// Cycle of Life: Realistic Fauna — FotSA canids (Caninae).
//
// These REPLACE vanilla wolf/fox. All auto-detected as predators (huntable-tag hunting) and most
// den. Group baselines with outlier tweaks — the sim cares that a wolf ≠ a fennec, not that two
// near-identical zorros differ by a day. Dens are left to auto-detection (canids genuinely den;
// solitary South American canids already lack a group spawn so never got one).
//
// preyPerPredator = standing prey needed per predator. LOW for omnivores (raccoon dogs, maned wolf,
// bat-eared/hoary foxes eat fruit/insects, so meat scarcity shouldn't starve them); higher for the
// big pack hunters. breedingMonths = birth months (pups in spring). predationVulnerability lower for
// pack animals (they defend), higher for lone small foxes.
//
// huntWhenFull = the fraction of the full kill rate a SATED canid keeps (0 = stops when full). True
// foxes (Vulpes) are THE textbook surplus killers — a red fox once killed 74 penguins, barely eating
// one — so they carry the strongest floor. Wolves/coyotes/jackals/dingoes surplus-kill opportunistically
// (deep snow, livestock), a modest floor. Insectivores (bat-eared fox), omnivores (raccoon dogs, maned
// wolf, South American zorros) and the rodent-specialist Ethiopian wolf keep 0 — they don't do it.
